The C#/JavaScript porting mistake `:CATCH oEx;`. catch_clause_form fires
on the would-be exception variable and points at GetLastSSLError(); the
:TRY block itself is otherwise well formed (diag.catch_clause_form).
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE SafeDivide;
	:PARAMETERS nNumerator, nDenominator;
	:DECLARE nResult;
	:TRY;
		nResult := nNumerator / nDenominator;
	:CATCH oEx;
		nResult := 0;
		ErrorMes("SafeDivide", oEx:Description);
	:ENDTRY;
	:RETURN nResult;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE SafeDivide;
	:PARAMETERS nNumerator, nDenominator;
	:DECLARE nResult;
	:TRY;
		nResult := nNumerator / nDenominator;
	:CATCH oEx;
		nResult := 0;
		ErrorMes("SafeDivide", oEx:Description);
	:ENDTRY;
	:RETURN nResult;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
6:9-6:12 error catch_clause_form: ':CATCH' does not take an exception variable; call 'GetLastSSLError()' inside the block instead
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
6:9-6:12 error catch_clause_form: ':CATCH' does not take an exception variable; call 'GetLastSSLError()' inside the block instead
6:9-6:12 warning undeclared_variable: Variable 'oEx' is not declared
